tests/ui/types/err_literal_tag_not_positive_definite.sky:1:36: error: `[[1, 2], [2, 1]]` is not known to be PositiveDefinite
  |
1 | P: PositiveDefinite Matrix[2, 2] = [[1, 2], [2, 1]]
  |                                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is Matrix[2,2] [1]
  |    ----------------------------- expected because of this annotation
  |                                                 - diagonal entry 1
  = note: the checker only knows a matrix property if it can prove it: from a declaration, or an operation that preserves it
  = note: the leading 2x2 block is not positive definite (its Cholesky pivot is -3)
  = help: fix the entries; only `ᵀ` and `⁻¹` keep PositiveDefinite; for a matrix you know is positive definite, pass it to a function whose parameter is declared PositiveDefinite: its symmetry is checked when the function is called, and its positivity by the Cholesky solve that relies on it

