tests/ui/types/err_literal_tag_not_positive_definite.sky:3:30: error: `[[1, 0], [0, 1]]` is not known to be Orthogonal
  |
3 | O: Orthogonal Matrix[2, 2] = [[1, 0], [0, 1]]
  |                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is Matrix[2,2] [1]
  |    ----------------------- expected because of this annotation
  = note: the checker only knows a matrix property if it can prove it: from a declaration, or an operation that preserves it
  = note: the checker never proves Orthogonal from a literal: exact orthogonality needs exact sums of products, which decimal entries do not give
  = help: build it from `identity(n)` and products and negations of Orthogonal matrices: an Orthogonal promise is never checked when the program runs, so the checker must know it
